### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal example of an HTML card that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the size, colors, or rotation angle to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D transforms */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover state – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Optional: add a back face for a flip‑card effect */
.card::before,
.card::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  backface-visibility: hidden;
  border-radius: 12px;
}

.card::before { /* Front face */
  background: #fff;
}

.card::after { /* Back face */
  background: #f8f8f8;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front content -->
    <div style="padding: 20px;">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
      <p>Hover over this card to see it rotate.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` sets a perspective so that 3D transforms look realistic.
2. **Transform‑style** – `preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3D space.
3. **Transition** – `transform 0.6s ease` animates the rotation smoothly.
4. **Hover** – On hover, the card rotates 180 degrees around the Y‑axis (`rotateY(180deg)`).

You can replace the content inside the card with images, text, or any other elements you like. If you want a flip‑card effect (showing a different back side), uncomment the `::before` and `::after` pseudo‑elements and style them accordingly.
